    "## Cell 7c — Anchor Scout (contact sheet)\n",
    "\n",
    "Low-altitude, featureless frames (e.g. plain grass) make terrible anchors. Skim\n",
    "this grid, note the `frame_idx` of ~10–15 frames with clear satellite-visible\n",
    "landmarks (roads, path junctions, building corners, field edges), then mark\n",
    "those in Cell 7b's `MANUAL_ANCHORS`. Each thumbnail is labelled with its altitude\n",
    "from the SRT — higher altitude = wider ground view = generally easier to match."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "286f5b46",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
